statement:
Let $k\subseteq k'$ be an extension [def-pc-field-extension] of algebraically closed fields and let $C$ be a curve over $k$ [def-sc-curves]. Let $C_{k'}=C\times_{\operatorname{Spec}k}\operatorname{Spec}k'$ be the base change [def-pc-base-change], a scheme over $k'$ through its second projection. Then:
1. $C_{k'}$ is a curve over $k'$, i.e. separated and of finite type over $k'$, and $\dim C_{k'}=\dim C$ (in particular $\dim C_{k'}\le1$);
2. if $C$ is smooth (resp. proper, resp. affine) over $k$, then $C_{k'}$ is smooth (resp. proper, resp. affine) over $k'$;
3. if $C$ is a connected curve (nonempty, connected, of dimension one), then $C_{k'}$ is a connected curve over $k'$.
